  "prediction": "**Mexico's Military Embroiled in Controversy Over Extrajudicial Killings**\n\nA disturbing video has surfaced in Mexico, appearing to show a soldier executing a civilian lying face down in the street with a shot to the back of his head. The footage, released by Mexican media outlets, purportedly depicts part of the military's encounter with fuel pipeline thieves in the central state of Puebla on May 3, 2017. The incident has sparked widespread condemnation and calls for an investigation.\n\nAccording to the video, a silver four-door car was ambushed by soldiers, and its occupants were forced to exit the vehicle. One of the men, who appears to be still alive, is dragged to a well-lit area and lies on the ground for six minutes before a soldier shoots him in the back of the head. The Mexican National Human Rights Commission has obtained a copy of the video and is urging a swift and thorough investigation.\n\nThe Mexican defense ministry has also urged federal prosecutors to investigate the incident, stating that the video must be \"irrefutably\" cleared up by federal investigators. The ministry has pledged to cooperate with the attorney general's office in the investigation.\n\nThis incident is not an isolated case, as Mexico's army has been embroiled in several scandals in recent years centering on the use of extrajudicial force. In 2014, soldiers were implicated in the killing of 22 suspects at a warehouse in the Mexico state community of Tlatlaya, with evidence suggesting that at least a dozen suspects were executed after they surrendered.\n\nThe video has sparked concerns about the use of extrajudicial force by the military in Mexico, which has been plagued by widespread gang violence and impunity. According to a report, Mexico had the second-highest number of murders last year among countries considered in \"armed conflicts.\" The government has disputed the report's findings, but the incident has highlighted the need for greater accountability and transparency in the military's actions.\n\nThe investigation into the incident is ongoing, and the Mexican government has promised to take swift action to address the allegations. However, the incident has raised concerns about the military's use of force and the need for greater oversight and accountability in Mexico.",
